# Rank 1719 / CVE-2020-2279: the Jenkins script-security plugin runs untrusted
# Groovy through the org.kohsuke:groovy-sandbox library, whose InvokerChain built
# its interceptor chain from a per-thread registry with no emptiness check, so
# sandbox-transformed code that ran on a thread without a registered interceptor
# took the unmediated fallback in every Checker.checked* branch and escaped the
# sandbox entirely (a script class overriding toString, returned to unsandboxed
# code). The plugin's own tree holds no vulnerable statement — the library
# coordinate is the whole evidence, so the pinned release is what the scan has to
# read. The fixed revision pins groovy-sandbox 1.27, whose InvokerChain substitutes a
# rejecting interceptor when the registry is empty.

test "rank1719: a groovy-sandbox pin below the fixed release is reported"
  lang java
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  file src/main/java/org/jenkinsci/plugins/scriptsecurity/sandbox/groovy/GroovySandbox.java
  code
  ```
  package org.jenkinsci.plugins.scriptsecurity.sandbox.groovy;

  public class GroovySandbox {
      public static void enter() {
      }
  }
  ```
  file pom.xml
  code
  ```
  <project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <groupId>org.jenkins-ci.plugins</groupId>
    <artifactId>script-security</artifactId>
    <version>1.74</version>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.kohsuke</groupId>
        <artifactId>groovy-sandbox</artifactId>
        <version>1.26</version>
        <exclusions>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.codehaus.groovy</groupId>
            <artifactId>groovy</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
        </exclusions>
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </project>
  ```

